# Snap_16 rows [1717, 8, 1517, 3115, 2069, 3321, 491, 14, 56]: Type, written Mvir (float) and
# SimulationHaloIndex (SAGE26 writes llabs of the halo's MostBoundID, src/io/save_gals_hdf5.c:878;
# none is negative) as MostBoundID, written Regime; Zcurr ZZ[16], snapnum 16. Each row enters the
# call with mergeType 0 (rows merge in the substeps, after the classification) and its input
# FFBRegime seeded to the opposite of the written value, so the write is visible.
# call.has_reference 1: the oracle refuses the fixture unless SAGE26's FFBRegime equals the
# written value of every row.
# Reachability: R6-reachable (real rows; the input FFBRegime seeded)
